H1 verification log (section: /home/claude/work/sections/H1_geometry.md)
Helion @ 5edd437f39ddcbcd647a305d7bdd306847d6686b, UZDoom @ 292cf4203ebd3ced951cb67f6819180f588c1d44

Corrections (old -> new, why):
1. Intro: "only GL 4.x features are persistent-mapped TBOs and glClipControl, both optional"
   -> adds the optional glMemoryBarrier (ARB_shader_image_load_store / 4.2) in the fuzz pass, cites Client.cs:282-288.
   Why: Client.cs:287 + LegacyWorldRenderer.cs:609-610 use it; the section itself lists it in 4.3.
2. 1.2: RenderWorldData.cs:183-206 -> RenderWorldData.cs:45-68.
   Why: the file has 85 lines; Draw()/Vbo.Upload() is at 45-68.
3. 1.2 code excerpt (LegacyWorldRenderer.cs:331-341): added the omitted profiler Start/Stop lines so it matches the file.
4. 2.1: "upper/lower skipped only if they are both Movement-dynamic and the side is dynamic"
   -> "only when an adjacent plane is flagged Movement and the side itself is dynamic (Side.IsDynamic = any flag)".
   Why: StaticCacheGeometryRenderer.cs:405-408 tests the plane Movement flags of either sector AND side.IsDynamic (Side.cs:48).
5. 2.3 SurfaceOptions: "texture-array layer (20 b)" -> "masked to 20 b but shifted to bit 13, so only the low 19 bits survive".
   Why: VertexOptions.cs:13 ((textureIndex & 0xFFFFF) << 13) = bits 13..32 in a 32-bit int.
6. 2.4: added the MaxArrayLayers split (GLTextureArrayBuilder.cs:218-240) to "one array per distinct dimension".
   Why: buckets larger than GLInfo.MaxArrayLayers are split into several arrays.
7. 2.6 code excerpt: rewrote it from the file (the old one merged statements and replaced code with comments); cite narrowed
   859-896 -> 864-892, plus VertexPipeline.cs:33-38 / VertexBufferObject.cs:14-21 for what Bind/DrawArrays do.
8. 3.2 code excerpt (GeometryRenderer.cs:904-925): added "..." where lines were left out (addAlpha, geometryType/arrayTexture).
9. 3.2: "Sector.CheckRenderingChanged does the same" -> "applies the gametick and Z tests (but not the RenderOffsets test)".
   Why: Sector.cs:245-257 has no RenderOffsets check, unlike SectorPlane.cs:98.
10. 5: "dist3D = (mvp·pos) means a second full mat4×vec4 on top of gl_Position"
   -> dist3D repeats gl_Position's mvp·pos (can be shared); the real extra multiply is mvpNoPitch for dist2D.
   Why: VertexFunction.cs:7 / InterpolationShader.cs:76 use the same mvp*mixPos; LightLevel.cs:30 uses mvpNoPitch.
   The dependent wording in the 5 Inference and in 10 row 9 was changed to match (Inference contradicted the code).
11. 5: "11 flat varyings plus 3-4 smooth" -> "15 flat plus 4 smooth (uvFrag, depthFrag, dist2D, dist3D)".
   Why: 10 flat in InterpolationShader.cs:34-43 + 2 uvClamp (VertexFunction.cs:9) + 2 sector colour/fog
   (SectorColorMap.cs:5-7) + lightLevelFrag (LightLevel.cs:20). Citations extended.
12. 6.1: "Four GLBufferTextureStorage TBOs are bound every frame" -> "Six ... (light, colormap, fog, colormap, map line data, line heights)".
   Why: Renderer.World.cs:37-42 declares six; Renderer.cs:551-556 binds six.
13. 6.2: noted that the non-persistent fallback also maps with MAP_UNSYNCHRONIZED_BIT (GLBufferTexture.cs:53);
   added map line data to the list of float TBOs that hit the element-vs-byte map-length bug (Renderer.World.cs:321-323).
14. 6.3: "Global and sector Boom colormaps ... (index,-1,-1)" -> "Per-sector Boom colormaps ...; SectorRgb stays an RGB multiplier".
   Why: Renderer.World.cs:264-306 writes sector.Colormap only (global/view colormap is a uniform); SectorRgb returns ColorMix at 302-303.
15. 7 VR hazard: "Both use a 32-unit pull-back" -> only the block/entity half-plane test uses it (LegacyWorldRenderer.cs:276-283, 784-786);
   the BSP BoxInFront test uses the MvpNoPitch near plane at the camera (LegacyWorldRenderer.Bsp.cs:19). Both are off when |pitch| > 45°.
16. 9: render.texturetransparency "Alpha middles via OIT" -> "Translucent (line alpha < 1) walls via OIT".
   Why: GeometryRenderer.cs:794-795 gates RenderAlphaSide on side.Line.Alpha < 1.

